Real World Example

Vendor wants:

Breakfast
Lunch
Dinner

Create meals:

Meal Table
id	name
1	Breakfast
2	Lunch
3	Dinner

Now vendor creates plans.

MealPlan Table
id	name
1	Breakfast Only
2	Lunch Only
3	Dinner Only
4	Breakfast + Lunch
5	Lunch + Dinner
6	Full Day

Connect meals to plans.

MealPlanItem
planId	mealId
1	1
2	2
3	3
4	1
4	2
5	2
5	3
6	1
6	2
6	3

Visual Representation

Breakfast Only
    |
    └── Breakfast

Lunch Only
    |
    └── Lunch

Dinner Only
    |
    └── Dinner

Breakfast + Lunch
    |
    ├── Breakfast
    └── Lunch

Lunch + Dinner
    |
    ├── Lunch
    └── Dinner

Full Day
    |
    ├── Breakfast
    ├── Lunch
    └── Dinner
Pricing
MealPlanPrice
id	planId	duration	amount
1	1	MONTHLY	1500
2	2	MONTHLY	2000
3	3	MONTHLY	2000
4	4	MONTHLY	3000
5	5	MONTHLY	3500
6	6	MONTHLY	4500
Customer Screen

API returns:

[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "Breakfast Only",
    "meals": ["Breakfast"],
    "price": 1500
  },
  {
    "id": 4,
    "name": "Breakfast + Lunch",
    "meals": ["Breakfast", "Lunch"],
    "price": 3000
  },
  {
    "id": 6,
    "name": "Full Day",
    "meals": ["Breakfast", "Lunch", "Dinner"],
    "price": 4500
  }
]